  "id": "eyewitness-testimony",
  "term": "eyewitness testimony",
  "definition": "Eyewitness testimony is evidence given by a person about what they remember of a crime or other event they saw. In psychology, it is understood as memory-based evidence that can be important in court but may be affected by internal and external influences, raising questions about its reliability.",
